WEBVTT

00:33.590 --> 00:38.740
At that time, I couldn't understand the feeling of being in touch with people.

00:44.350 --> 00:49.860
At that time, I couldn't understand the feeling of being alone.

00:59.740 --> 01:02.210
Hey, Chihiro, let's go.

01:02.660 --> 01:03.160
Yeah.

01:05.160 --> 01:07.170
L-e-t's play!

01:08.670 --> 01:10.630
L-e-t's play!

01:17.090 --> 01:18.050
Let's go.

01:18.050 --> 01:20.890
E-Eh? Where are we going?

01:20.890 --> 01:22.310
Our place.

01:22.310 --> 01:24.060
W-Wait a second!

01:24.060 --> 01:28.560
That small encounter totally changed the path I was walking.

01:29.810 --> 01:33.820
I believed that the happy times would continue forever.

01:35.740 --> 01:36.490
But...

01:39.740 --> 01:42.580
Fly high, make it

01:42.580 --> 01:45.830
Get to the new world that I seek

01:46.080 --> 01:52.420
Someday with my little wings

01:52.590 --> 01:58.630
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

01:58.970 --> 02:04.850
Here's my real intention I hide

02:05.350 --> 02:11.560
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

02:11.770 --> 02:17.860
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

02:18.150 --> 02:23.870
I have been looking for my own style

02:23.870 --> 02:31.370
Don't give it up, here comes the life

02:34.250 --> 02:37.010
Be alive, take it

02:37.010 --> 02:40.260
Promise to find, yes I will

02:40.550 --> 02:46.720
Shining wings filled with wishes

02:47.060 --> 02:49.810
Fly high, make it

02:49.810 --> 02:53.270
Get to the new world that I seek

02:53.310 --> 02:59.780
Someday, so I believe

03:21.420 --> 03:22.470
Hey.

03:23.390 --> 03:25.390
Something is on my head.

03:25.390 --> 03:26.720
It's a present.

03:26.720 --> 03:27.720
Present?

03:28.810 --> 03:30.480
Sorry about the day before yesterday.

03:30.480 --> 03:32.140
I broke our promise.

03:32.140 --> 03:34.650
Ah, it seems that way, though...

03:34.650 --> 03:35.560
Though?

03:35.560 --> 03:39.900
The truth is, I don't really remember what happened back then.

03:40.150 --> 03:41.150
Oh...

03:41.490 --> 03:44.030
But thank you very much.

03:48.450 --> 03:49.200
Pya?

03:51.250 --> 03:52.540
What's wrong?

03:52.540 --> 03:54.580
N-Nothing.

03:54.580 --> 03:58.000
It's cute. Thank you very much.

03:58.000 --> 03:59.210
Is your cold better?

04:01.800 --> 04:04.970
Yes, it's fine.

04:04.970 --> 04:08.180
I see. I'm glad that you've recovered.

04:12.600 --> 04:13.560
Say.

04:13.560 --> 04:14.810
What is it?

04:15.400 --> 04:17.230
There's something I want to talk to you about.

04:20.110 --> 04:22.610
Do you want to write a novel with me?

04:24.610 --> 04:25.570
Eh?

04:27.780 --> 04:31.290
Why did you ask that?

04:31.700 --> 04:33.250
"Why...?"

04:33.250 --> 04:35.750
Doesn't it sound fun? Let's try to write one.

04:36.080 --> 04:37.040
It's impossible.

04:37.040 --> 04:39.250
There's no way I can do it.

04:39.250 --> 04:40.420
Why?

04:40.420 --> 04:41.590
"Why?"

04:42.510 --> 04:48.260
You know that my memory doesn't last more than thirteen hours, right?

04:48.550 --> 04:49.430
Yeah.

04:49.430 --> 04:51.100
But I'll help you too...

04:51.100 --> 04:52.930
I don't want to write one.

04:52.930 --> 04:54.270
No way...

04:54.680 --> 04:57.440
Why did you say something so mean?

04:57.440 --> 04:59.690
Mean? Me?

04:59.690 --> 05:03.230
Yes. You're usually a much kinder person.

05:03.530 --> 05:08.200
I want to try writing a novel for your sake.

05:08.870 --> 05:11.200
Why is it for my sake?

05:11.780 --> 05:16.370
Because you said it was your dream to write stories.

05:17.620 --> 05:19.130
DREAM

05:19.420 --> 05:22.380
That was the me from a week ago.

05:22.750 --> 05:26.130
You are you, whether from a week ago or now.

05:26.130 --> 05:27.720
A dream is a dream.

05:29.090 --> 05:30.350
I'm going home.

05:31.470 --> 05:32.390
Chihiro!

05:35.890 --> 05:40.690
Somehow I don't understand you anymore.

05:41.730 --> 05:43.940
That's natural.

05:43.940 --> 05:45.940
Even I don't understand myself anymore.

05:49.950 --> 05:54.490
You broke your promise to me because you met Miyamura-senpai?

05:56.120 --> 05:57.160
Idiot.

06:08.380 --> 06:09.880
Ah, Kei-senpai?

06:09.880 --> 06:12.050
Let's trade this month's manga.

06:12.050 --> 06:14.850
Ah, sorry. I haven't bought mine yet.

06:14.850 --> 06:16.100
Eh?!

06:16.100 --> 06:19.230
You're in charge of getting the monthly magazine, MIMI.

06:19.230 --> 06:23.650
Sorry. You can go ahead and read it first, so you buy it.

06:23.650 --> 06:26.650
I'm out of money already for the month.

06:26.650 --> 06:28.860
I lent some to Hiro-senpai the other day too.

06:28.860 --> 06:29.650
Eh?

06:30.490 --> 06:32.120
Why did Onii-chan borrow money from you?

06:32.120 --> 06:35.450
Because Hiro-senpai was dumped by Miyamura-senpai.

06:35.450 --> 06:36.450
Huh?

06:36.450 --> 06:41.580
Hiro-senpai was penniless, so I paid the bill for him.

06:41.580 --> 06:44.210
I don't understand what you're talking about at all.

06:44.840 --> 06:48.760
In other words, Miyamura-senpai was supposed to treat Hiro-senpai the day before yesterday.

06:48.970 --> 06:52.260
Hiro-senpai made her mad, and she went home early.

06:52.260 --> 06:54.390
Then Onii-chan is...

06:54.390 --> 06:59.730
Hiro-senpai is as clumsy in relationships with girls as he seems.

07:00.230 --> 07:01.350
I see.

07:08.650 --> 07:11.030
It flies pretty well, because it's light.

07:13.030 --> 07:15.530
Can't I get paid soon?

07:20.330 --> 07:21.460
Miyamura?

07:23.000 --> 07:25.790
Ah, erm... Miyako-san.

07:25.790 --> 07:27.500
Don't add "san" either.

07:27.500 --> 07:29.380
Next time I won't answer you.

07:29.630 --> 07:30.720
Okay.

07:30.720 --> 07:31.760
Good.

07:31.760 --> 07:36.180
Because of your obedience, I guess I'll make an exception and forgive you this time.

07:36.180 --> 07:39.520
Forgive? Did I do something that bad?

07:39.810 --> 07:41.730
Hirono-kun, what's that?

07:42.020 --> 07:45.650
I know. It's some extraordinary food prepared for our reunion.

07:45.650 --> 07:49.610
That's right. My credit is always in an extraordinary state at the end of the month.

07:49.610 --> 07:51.610
Poor you.

07:52.240 --> 07:53.110
That's right.

07:54.110 --> 07:57.200
This time I'll treat you for real, so let's go and eat something.

07:57.200 --> 07:59.660
I can't just go strolling around every day.

07:59.660 --> 08:01.450
I have work to do.

08:01.700 --> 08:03.710
Even though it's Sunday?

08:03.710 --> 08:05.630
That doesn't matter.

08:05.630 --> 08:06.500
I see.

08:07.040 --> 08:08.090
Well then...

08:09.670 --> 08:10.510
Let's go.

08:10.510 --> 08:11.800
Where are we going?

08:12.090 --> 08:14.340
Your place of course.

08:14.590 --> 08:15.590
Huh?

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Aoki Ookami

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Twilight Mystery

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Shiroki Stejika

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
The NEET Next Door

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Yamada Hajimemashite

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Tamago Suubu

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Idete Mako

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
The Lid of Pandora's Box

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
Sakura Mokomoko

08:17.220 --> 08:18.220
• Shindou Nagi

08:19.260 --> 08:20.260
List price 540 yen

08:19.260 --> 08:20.260
• Recipes for Night Meals that
Won't Cause Weight Gain
• Miso Soup of Love
• Beef Impact

08:19.260 --> 08:20.260
Asian Taste

08:19.260 --> 08:20.260
• Bistro Shaft
• Very Cute Cookware
Aune Machine

08:19.260 --> 08:20.260
YAM SPECIAL EDITION

08:20.560 --> 08:24.520
I'm sure he doesn't have anything good to eat, since it's the end of the month.

08:25.230 --> 08:26.270
All right.

08:33.360 --> 08:35.240
If I remember correctly, that girl is Hirono's...

08:41.080 --> 08:42.330
So it was her.

08:44.620 --> 08:48.170
Heh, you live in quite a nice place.

08:48.170 --> 08:51.340
Shouldn't you be a little more cautious?

08:51.590 --> 08:53.090
Eh? Why?

08:53.510 --> 08:55.430
You're a girl after all.

08:55.430 --> 08:58.850
You shouldn't just go to a guy's room like it's nothing.

08:58.850 --> 09:01.140
It's okay. I know.

09:01.140 --> 09:02.060
What?

09:02.390 --> 09:05.980
That you'll be nice to me.

09:06.440 --> 09:09.860
Your thinking is too naive.

09:09.860 --> 09:12.650
That response doesn't sound right.

09:12.650 --> 09:17.160
With someone you don't know well, there's no way you could know.

09:17.160 --> 09:21.620
I know what kind of person he is and what he's thinking.

09:21.620 --> 09:22.660
Liar.

09:22.660 --> 09:26.120
I'm not bragging, but I have a good eye for people.

09:26.330 --> 09:28.500
Because, I...

09:29.460 --> 09:30.630
What?

09:30.630 --> 09:33.880
Ha! I found an ecchi book!

09:34.170 --> 09:37.340
Heh, so that's what you're into.

09:37.340 --> 09:38.890
This is drawing material.

09:38.890 --> 09:41.800
Oh, like that sounds plausible.

09:42.680 --> 09:45.430
I want to do my work soon.

09:45.430 --> 09:49.270
Ah, go ahead. Don't mind me.

09:49.270 --> 09:51.150
I'll observe quietly.

09:51.150 --> 09:55.150
Listen, I can't let others see my drafts before they're published.

09:55.150 --> 09:58.070
Then show me some that have already been published.

09:58.530 --> 10:00.450
Lend me the manga that you drew.

10:00.700 --> 10:02.870
If you do that, I'll go home immediately.

10:02.870 --> 10:05.120
Why do I have to make a deal with you?

10:05.410 --> 10:07.710
S-h-o-w me.

10:09.040 --> 10:10.710
I guess I have no choice.

10:12.630 --> 10:15.170
This is a short story I wrote before my works were serialized.

10:15.170 --> 10:18.510
It hasn't been published as a book yet, so I only have copies of it.

10:18.510 --> 10:19.430
That's great.

10:19.800 --> 10:21.720
Then I'm borrowing it.

10:21.720 --> 10:23.180
FILM RESEARCH CLUB

10:24.060 --> 10:25.060
Kyosuke.

10:25.470 --> 10:28.140
Sorry, President. I'm taking my camera.

10:28.140 --> 10:29.060
I see.

10:29.440 --> 10:31.480
Let me know if you're short of equipment.

10:31.480 --> 10:35.020
Thank you. I think I'll probably ask you before the next production.

10:35.020 --> 10:36.110
The Cinema Festival.

10:37.150 --> 10:41.740
The guys were bragging about it, so they'll definitely win.

10:42.110 --> 10:44.370
What about you? Are you going to make one by yourself?

10:45.160 --> 10:45.660
Yeah.

10:46.120 --> 10:48.410
There's a film I want to make no matter what.

11:03.590 --> 11:05.890
How is it, Mizuki? Is it good?

11:07.270 --> 11:10.230
That's quite an arrogant question.

11:11.310 --> 11:16.270
This isn't about deliciousness. It's about whether eating it will be harmful or not.

11:17.230 --> 11:18.230
Is it that bad?

11:18.650 --> 11:22.780
How on earth can you make such bad food?

11:23.030 --> 11:25.530
You don't need to put it like that.

11:25.530 --> 11:30.500
Even though it's just one, you shouldn't waste rice like this.

11:30.500 --> 11:32.750
It's not one. It's three.

11:32.750 --> 11:33.120
Yes?

11:33.370 --> 11:36.960
I made three. This is the rice ball that got finished.

11:38.000 --> 11:40.380
Where are the other two?

11:40.380 --> 11:42.300
They stuck to my hands while I was molding them.

11:45.140 --> 11:48.680
You shouldn't cook, ever again!

11:48.680 --> 11:51.230
Don't be so mad.

11:51.230 --> 11:53.640
Anyway, what happened all of a sudden?

11:53.640 --> 11:56.110
It's not like you to cook.

11:56.110 --> 12:00.440
Because... I'm responsible for it too.

12:00.740 --> 12:01.570
Huh?

12:01.570 --> 12:03.360
Nah, it's nothing.

12:04.610 --> 12:05.620
• Shindou Nagi

12:05.620 --> 12:10.580
It's also partly my fault that Onii-chan is working so hard now.

12:13.160 --> 12:14.670
"Flower and Snake" is a parody of an erotic literature's title of the same pronounciation (花と蛇), written by Dan Oniroku.

12:15.040 --> 12:19.380
Onii-chan, look! This one is interesting too. Read it.

12:17.840 --> 12:19.380
The Fire Too Serious
Living For Life
Day-by-day With Tears

12:17.840 --> 12:22.550
"Masquerade" is another parody of a martial art manga of the same pronounciation drawn by Itagaki Masaya.

12:19.380 --> 12:20.130
Okay.

12:20.500 --> 12:22.550
Ah, wait a second.

12:27.890 --> 12:29.140
Amazing!

12:29.510 --> 12:31.430
Wow. It looks exactly the same.

12:31.430 --> 12:33.890
Hey, draw more.

12:33.890 --> 12:34.560
All right.

12:35.560 --> 12:37.860
You might be a genius.

12:37.860 --> 12:39.110
I... wonder.

12:40.230 --> 12:41.820
Amazing.

12:43.150 --> 12:47.240
At that time, I was happy to be with Onii-chan.

12:48.700 --> 12:52.540
At that time, I was happy to see them happy.

12:53.250 --> 12:55.250
But, now...

12:57.880 --> 13:01.000
What am I seeking now?

13:01.670 --> 13:06.720
I'm searching for the color that's missing from the world I see. I...

13:11.930 --> 13:12.770
Hirono-kun.

13:16.480 --> 13:18.150
When did you come in?

13:18.150 --> 13:21.020
More importantly, Hirono-kun. Manga.

13:21.020 --> 13:23.820
Huh? I'm drawing it right now.

13:23.820 --> 13:26.400
Not that one. The others.

13:26.400 --> 13:29.120
Do you have any other manga that you drew?

13:29.120 --> 13:34.160
Yeah. I still have three more short stories, and the ones that were serialized already.

13:34.160 --> 13:36.080
Lend me those. Right now.

13:36.460 --> 13:40.750
"Right now"? Is my manga that interesting?

13:40.750 --> 13:42.880
Eh? Hmm...

13:53.010 --> 13:55.390
Hirono-kun, you're being nervous.

13:55.890 --> 13:56.730
Shut up!

13:57.730 --> 14:00.690
Well, they were <i>really interesting.</i>

14:01.610 --> 14:03.820
You might be a genius.

14:11.410 --> 14:12.700
Hi. Hello.

14:12.700 --> 14:18.540
Ah, Mizuki. The pork cutlet is still raw inside, even though the outside is burned black.

14:18.540 --> 14:21.710
Is it the pan's fault?

14:21.710 --> 14:23.790
It's your fault.

14:23.790 --> 14:27.010
Don't be mean to me. Teach me.

14:27.010 --> 14:31.260
Listen, Senpai. For fried food, the temperature of the oil...

14:30.550 --> 14:32.930
Ah, fire! Fire!

14:33.760 --> 14:35.890
The pan is burning!

14:36.970 --> 14:38.680
Water! Water! Water!

14:38.680 --> 14:42.860
Nah, don't use water! Absolutely not! The fire will only get stronger!

14:42.860 --> 14:44.440
Then what should I do?

14:45.860 --> 14:48.240
Mayonnaise. Put mayonnaise on it.

14:48.240 --> 14:50.200
Pour a whole ton of it into the pan.

14:50.200 --> 14:52.320
A whole ton of it...? H-Hold on a second.

14:54.870 --> 14:57.080
Senpai? Senpai?

15:00.540 --> 15:01.330
The fire is out.

15:02.170 --> 15:05.340
The fire is out, Mizuki! You're an amazing genius!

15:06.840 --> 15:09.090
I'm not an amazing genius!

15:13.050 --> 15:15.180
Ah, a new record.

15:17.600 --> 15:18.810
Welcome back.

15:19.770 --> 15:21.100
It's not "welcome back".

15:21.100 --> 15:24.980
It'd be better if you stopped hiding the duplicate key under the flowerpot.

15:26.520 --> 15:28.780
What are you doing?

15:28.780 --> 15:32.570
I'm thinking of making you dinner to thank you for the manga.

15:32.570 --> 15:33.860
Go home, you.

15:33.860 --> 15:34.820
Why?

15:35.120 --> 15:39.450
Do you know that humans can't digest raw starch?

15:40.160 --> 15:40.750
Yes?

15:41.040 --> 15:45.250
Do you know that an excessive intake of chemical seasonings makes your hands and feet go numb?

15:45.540 --> 15:47.040
So what are you trying to say?

15:47.420 --> 15:51.880
I decided I wouldn't eat a girl's home cooking as long as I lived.

15:53.220 --> 15:56.260
It seems you have some kind of dark past.

15:56.260 --> 15:58.220
It's fine. It's none of your business.

15:58.220 --> 16:01.140
The only food that my heart allows are these!

16:04.060 --> 16:08.110
All right, Miyako's specially-made rice with wild herbs is ready!

16:08.110 --> 16:10.110
So? Are you going to try it?

16:17.450 --> 16:18.580
It's delicious, isn't it?

16:20.410 --> 16:21.250
Delicious?

16:21.250 --> 16:22.710
Yeah, it's good.

16:22.710 --> 16:23.750
See?

16:23.750 --> 16:27.500
Damn it. She's the only one I didn't want to flatter.

16:27.500 --> 16:31.800
It's some compensation if you say it's delicious.

16:31.800 --> 16:34.180
It's not worth making if I'm eating alone.

16:34.630 --> 16:37.050
Alone...? What about your family?

16:37.050 --> 16:38.850
You shouldn't, Hirono-kun.

16:39.260 --> 16:41.180
The way you hold your chopsticks is weird.

16:41.180 --> 16:45.520
Since you're Japanese, you have to hold chopsticks properly.

16:47.060 --> 16:49.570
I have tendonitis in my right hand.

16:50.650 --> 16:52.650
Sorry, I didn't know.

16:52.650 --> 16:55.950
Don't worry about it. It's something like an occupational hazard.

16:55.950 --> 16:57.110
Is it serious?

16:57.110 --> 16:58.370
It's a light case.

16:58.370 --> 17:02.620
There are people who only draw when the pain abates, but I'm not that badly off.

17:03.000 --> 17:05.210
Hmm, that's terrible.

17:05.500 --> 17:07.000
How should I put it?

17:07.000 --> 17:12.630
It is terrible. Not sleeping, not eating. Can't have fun, and can't go to school.

17:12.880 --> 17:14.130
That's...

17:14.550 --> 17:16.300
What do you think?

17:16.630 --> 17:17.470
"What do I think?"

17:18.010 --> 17:22.930
Do I look like an idiot who's forcing himself to do the impossible?

17:27.230 --> 17:28.520
That's not true.

17:30.440 --> 17:34.360
Just doing your best makes it worthwhile.

17:35.990 --> 17:38.110
Hirono-kun's not an idiot.

17:39.660 --> 17:41.530
What are you doing?

17:41.830 --> 17:43.580
You can't hold the chopsticks, right?

17:44.700 --> 17:46.790
It's okay. I can eat by myself.

17:47.080 --> 17:48.210
No.

17:48.210 --> 17:51.920
If you want to do your work, you have to let your hand rest a bit.

17:51.920 --> 17:53.300
Here. Ah.

17:53.300 --> 17:55.300
Stop it. It's fine.

17:55.300 --> 17:57.300
It's not. Ah.

17:58.050 --> 17:59.300
What're you doing?

18:01.550 --> 18:02.300
Kei.

18:11.360 --> 18:12.310
Kei...

18:14.730 --> 18:17.400
Wait, Chihiro. Why not?

18:23.160 --> 18:24.990
Give the novel a try.

18:24.990 --> 18:26.750
Didn't you say it's your dream?

18:26.750 --> 18:27.450
Eh?

18:27.870 --> 18:30.790
Didn't you say there are stories you want to write?

18:31.170 --> 18:32.540
I'll help you too.

18:33.790 --> 18:36.630
Do you think you're saying something nice?

18:38.920 --> 18:41.890
Do you think you're saying something cool?

18:42.890 --> 18:45.600
Since I'm a person who's come to a dead end,

18:45.600 --> 18:48.430
since there's nothing I want to or can do,

18:48.430 --> 18:50.810
that's why it's okay if my dream comes true.

18:51.650 --> 18:54.480
Such a simple...

19:02.240 --> 19:03.370
You're right.

19:03.780 --> 19:04.620
Chihiro...

19:05.280 --> 19:09.120
You're the one who's right. I'm the one who's wrong.

19:09.660 --> 19:13.380
But even so, what do you want me to do?

19:33.310 --> 19:34.360
Help me.

19:35.650 --> 19:36.730
Why?

19:38.530 --> 19:43.280
Why does someone else know me better than I know myself?!

19:49.080 --> 19:50.450
I want to write.

19:51.290 --> 19:52.870
To tell you the truth, I want to write.

19:53.250 --> 19:57.500
That's the only dream left before my memory disappears.

19:58.090 --> 20:00.300
But I really don't want to.

20:00.300 --> 20:01.170
Why?

20:01.470 --> 20:02.930
I'm scared.

20:02.930 --> 20:08.430
If even that doesn't work out, then I really will have nothing left, won't I?

20:09.430 --> 20:11.560
I see. Sorry.

20:11.980 --> 20:12.560
Yeah.

20:16.810 --> 20:20.030
Erm, can I kiss you?

20:20.030 --> 20:22.780
Kissing is something lovers do.

20:23.030 --> 20:25.280
Can't we become lovers?

20:25.280 --> 20:30.290
You're mean today, so no.

20:30.290 --> 20:31.370
I see.

20:31.750 --> 20:33.620
Yesterday, I would've been glad to.

20:35.080 --> 20:38.750
I felt really lonely sleeping by myself last night.

20:38.750 --> 20:43.300
I wanted to see you, and... I loved you.

20:44.630 --> 20:47.890
The me from yesterday wrote that in my diary.

20:47.890 --> 20:50.810
Really? That's a pity.

20:50.810 --> 20:55.350
I dislike today's you. But I don't hate you.

20:56.310 --> 20:58.730
Please hug me for a bit longer.

20:58.730 --> 20:59.900
Hug?

20:59.900 --> 21:01.650
Yes. It's warm.

21:02.070 --> 21:03.150
Chihiro.

21:03.150 --> 21:03.940
Yes.

21:03.940 --> 21:06.740
What kind of story do you want to write?

21:07.070 --> 21:09.410
Geez, you're persistent.

21:09.410 --> 21:10.240
Tell me.

21:10.910 --> 21:13.500
What I'm thinking about writing is...

21:14.830 --> 21:21.250
a story about a girl who's the only survivor in a world where everything's been destroyed.

21:42.980 --> 21:49.740
furimukeba soba ni iru kara

21:42.980 --> 21:49.740
Since you're by my side when I turn around,

21:50.780 --> 21:56.330
sunao ni narenokute

21:50.780 --> 21:56.330
I could not be honest

21:56.460 --> 21:58.790
itsuka wa

21:56.460 --> 21:58.790
Because someday

21:59.170 --> 22:05.420
yureru watashi no kono omoi wo

21:59.170 --> 22:12.100
I want to convey the feelings of my wavering self

22:06.010 --> 22:12.100
tsutaetai kara

22:12.510 --> 22:21.900
kawaranai toki anata no koe

22:12.510 --> 22:21.900
The unchanging time, your voice,

22:21.980 --> 22:29.490
yasashisa wa setsunakute

22:21.980 --> 22:29.490
Your kindness is suffocating

22:29.490 --> 22:37.870
fuan na hitomi tomadoi kakushi

22:29.490 --> 22:37.870
I'm hiding the confusion in my uneasy eyes

22:37.960 --> 22:44.710
egao ga itakute

22:37.960 --> 22:44.710
It hurts to smile

22:54.350 --> 22:55.810
Kei-senpai!

22:57.100 --> 22:59.480
What are you doing, Senpai?

22:59.480 --> 23:00.770
Nothing.

23:00.770 --> 23:02.690
What's wrong with that?

23:03.110 --> 23:04.270
Nothing.

23:04.770 --> 23:06.610
Can I have one?

23:09.190 --> 23:11.660
Geez, this is no good, Senpai.

23:11.660 --> 23:13.160
If you don't put something on it,

23:13.660 --> 23:16.240
the bread becomes soggy after absorbing water from the vegetables...

23:19.290 --> 23:20.660
Senpai?

23:22.120 --> 23:23.250
It's nothing.

23:28.050 --> 23:31.260
The woven story is a lonely one.

23:32.180 --> 23:35.850
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories:

23:36.180 --> 23:37.310
Outline.

23:38.100 --> 23:41.390
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
